From 0d303123353418e98eaaea3ab18fea115449984f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:06:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ss-delta: unlock the add-ons by recording them in the save's
 system.bin

The game reads what was bought on PSN from system.bin: after a 32-byte
header, four sorted id lists (add-on pacts, parts, items, raiments) and a
CRC-32/BZIP2 check over the file with the check zeroed. At start,
ss-delta.exe ([game] dlc, now on) adds the released add-ons' ids to the
player's own system.bin/.bak, keeping what is there, once the installed
game has the add-on pacts (quest_param.csv rows to 580) and raiments
(costume_table.csv row 130); the previous files go to
ss-delta/save-backups/. The result is byte-identical to the system.bin
Vita owners swap in, and the new raiments appear.

Reverts the offline PSN entitlement HLE of the previous commit: the game
holds those entitlements but only hands them out after an online step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
